  :from ~/.claude.bak.2026-04-27/projects/-Users-josephwecker-v2-src-agentic-systems/6da0db68-edec-474a-855f-afb0676d1c8f.jsonl#2026-04-24T17:42:43-06:00
  :project agentic-systems

  |title Assume the burden of proof is on the reviewer

  |quote
    Do not report a problem until you have checked whether the repo already acknowledges, narrows, or resolves it elsewhere. Note where the framing is wrong or inadequate, but
          otherwise deprioritize any obviously known qualifications and issues. Assume the burden of proof is on the reviewer. A finding only counts if you can show both the
      problematic
          passage and the strongest available mitigating passage, then explain why
            the issue still stands or does not.

  |occasion
    The standing text of the de-novo audit brief, re-pasted into the session so it would
    be fresh — the same message as #exm-sample-before-you-fixate.

  |about
    An audit standard that inverts the usual asymmetry. A finding is not a suspicion
    that survived; it is a two-sided exhibit — the problematic passage **and** the
    strongest mitigating passage the repository itself offers — plus an argument for why
    the issue still stands against it. This makes the cheap move (noticing something
    that looks wrong) not a finding at all, and it is the mechanism behind the estate's
    charitable-reading discipline rather than an exhortation toward it.

  |before-acting
    - You have found something that looks wrong and are about to report it.
    - You are writing up a finding and have not looked for what already addresses it.
    - You are reviewing work and your confidence is coming from the defect being
      obvious.

  |see
    - #exm-sample-before-you-fixate
    - #exm-assume-you-are-wrong

  |working-notes
    The carved span preserves the primary's ragged indentation, which is an artifact of
    how the block was pasted rather than of his typing. Left as-is per FORMAT D6
    (verbatim, not reformatted) — but flagged, because it is the one span in this
    harvest where faithfulness and readability genuinely pull apart, and a reviewer may
    reasonably decide the paste artifact is not part of the utterance.

    Located with `memorata3-search` and carved from the primary by anchored span
    extraction (never retyped); verified back against the primary byte-for-byte after
    emission.
